      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes complete sense that you'd see it that way—when every chapter feels the same, your mind starts writing the ending for you. But a story isn't just its plot; it's also the quiet moments between chapters, and those can change without you even noticing. The weight feels permanent because it's been there so long, but that doesn't mean it's a fact—it's a feeling, and feelings shift. You don't have to believe it right now, but you don't have to decide the ending today either. Just pause the story for tonight, and let someone else hold the pen for a while.",
